---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./dunstkreis.css";

const PANELS = [
    {
        name: "sky",
        title: "Sky",
        note: "cube map in cd/m², without the sun disc; lower levels the mean of four texels",
    },
    {
        name: "irradiance",
        title: "Irradiance",
        note: "for every normal, in lux, from the nine coefficients; every level computed from them",
    },
];
---

<figure class="scene-frame" id="environment">
    <div class="lut-bar">
        <span class="note">faces</span>
        <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Cube map face size">
            {
                [32, 64, 128, 256, 512].map((n) => (
                    <label>
                        <input type="radio" name="environment-size" value={n} checked={n === 128} />
                        <span>{n}</span>
                    </label>
                ))
            }
        </span>
        <span class="note" data-field="timing"></span>
    </div>
    {
        PANELS.map((panel) => (
            <section class="lut" data-panel={panel.name}>
                <p class="lut-head">
                    <strong>{panel.title}</strong> <span class="note">{panel.note}</span>
                </p>
                <p class="lut-controls">
                    <span class="note">mip level</span>
                    <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label={`${panel.title} mip level`} data-field="levels" />
                </p>
                <div class="lut-plot">
                    <span class="lut-axis lut-y">
                        <span>zenith</span>
                        <span>altitude, the horizon in the middle</span>
                        <span>nadir</span>
                    </span>
                    <div class="lut-stage" style="aspect-ratio: 2 / 1">
                        <canvas data-field="image" aria-label={`The ${panel.title.toLowerCase()} cube map, unrolled`} />
                    </div>
                    <span class="lut-axis lut-x">
                        <span>N</span>
                        <span>E · azimuth · S · W</span>
                        <span>N</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </section>
        ))
    }
    <p class="lut-values" data-field="sun"></p>
    <pre class="lut-values" data-field="sh"></pre>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Lighting a scene by this sky: the sky as a cube map, unrolled here into a panorama, the nine spherical harmonics
        coefficients of it, the irradiance they give every surface, and the sunlight that reaches the observer, which
        lights the scene as a light of its own. Tone mapped, each by its own scale.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./environment.js";
</script>
